Title: AI-Powered Regulatory Document Processing System for Aviation Compliance

Inventor: [Your Name]
Filing Date: [Current Date]
Application Type: Provisional Patent Application

TECHNICAL FIELD

This invention relates to artificial intelligence systems for processing regulatory documents in aviation training and compliance management, specifically utilizing natural language processing and machine learning for automated extraction and validation of regulatory data from aviation certificates and training records.

BACKGROUND OF THE INVENTION

Aviation training organizations must maintain comprehensive compliance with federal aviation regulations, particularly FAR Part 142 training center requirements. Current manual document processing methods are time-intensive, error-prone, and fail to provide systematic validation of regulatory compliance across diverse document formats.

Traditional approaches require manual data entry from pilot certificates, training records, and regulatory documents, leading to transcription errors, incomplete data capture, and inability to scale across international aviation markets with varying document formats and languages.

Existing document processing solutions lack aviation-specific regulatory knowledge, cannot handle complex aviation certificate formats with Roman numeral sections, and fail to provide confidence scoring for extracted data validation.

SUMMARY OF THE INVENTION

The present invention provides an AI-powered regulatory document processing system that automatically extracts, validates, and structures data from aviation regulatory documents using advanced natural language processing and machine learning algorithms.

The system utilizes OpenAI GPT-4o language models with specialized aviation regulatory prompting to identify and extract specific regulatory fields from diverse document formats, including FAA pilot certificates, training records, and international aviation credentials.

Key innovations include:
- Specialized aviation regulatory field mapping and extraction algorithms
- Roman numeral section parsing for FAA certificate formats
- Multi-language support for international aviation document processing
- Confidence scoring and validation mechanisms for extracted data
- Automated compliance gap identification and recommendations

DETAILED DESCRIPTION OF THE INVENTION

