Document Processing Pipeline:

1. Document Upload and Classification
   - Supports PDF, image, and text document formats
   - Automatic document type classification (pilot certificate, training record, etc.)
   - Multi-language document detection and routing

2. Optical Character Recognition (OCR)
   - Advanced OCR processing for scanned documents and images
   - Text extraction with position and formatting preservation
   - Quality assessment and error detection for OCR output

3. AI-Powered Field Extraction
   - OpenAI GPT-4o integration with aviation-specific prompt engineering
   - Specialized regulatory field mapping for FAA certificate sections
   - Roman numeral section parsing (I through XXVI for pilot certificates)
   - Confidence scoring for each extracted field

4. Data Validation and Structuring
   - Automated validation against known aviation data formats
   - Cross-reference validation with FAA databases
   - Structured output generation for database integration

Aviation-Specific Processing Methods:

A. FAA Pilot Certificate Processing
   The system processes FAA pilot certificates by identifying and extracting data from specific Roman numeral sections:
   - Section I: Certificate number and type
   - Section II: Name and date of birth
   - Section III: Nationality and address
   - Sections IV-XXVI: Ratings, limitations, and endorsements

B. Training Record Processing
   - Automated extraction of flight hours, training dates, and instructor information
   - Validation against FAR Part 61 and Part 142 requirements
   - Integration with training progression tracking

C. International Document Support
   - ICAO standard document format recognition
   - Multi-language text extraction and translation
   - International aviation authority credential validation

AI Processing Methodology:

The system employs specialized prompt engineering for aviation regulatory processing:

1. Context-Aware Prompting
   - Aviation regulatory context establishment
   - Document type-specific processing instructions
   - Field extraction templates for consistent output formatting

2. Confidence Scoring Algorithm
   - Multi-factor confidence assessment based on text clarity, field consistency, and regulatory validation
   - Threshold-based flagging for manual review requirements
   - Continuous learning from user validation feedback

3. Error Detection and Correction
   - Automated detection of common OCR errors in aviation documents
   - Context-based correction using aviation regulatory knowledge
   - Flagging of potentially invalid or suspicious data

Technical Implementation Details:

A. Natural Language Processing Pipeline
   - Pre-processing for aviation document formatting
   - Named entity recognition for aviation-specific terms
   - Relationship extraction between regulatory fields

B. Machine Learning Integration
   - Continuous improvement through user feedback integration
   - Model fine-tuning for specific aviation document types
   - Performance optimization for processing speed and accuracy

C. API Integration Framework
   - RESTful API for document processing requests
   - Webhook support for asynchronous processing notifications
   - Integration capabilities with existing aviation management systems

Data Security and Compliance:

The system implements comprehensive security measures:
