CLAIMS

1. A method for processing aviation regulatory documents comprising:
   a) Receiving digital documents containing aviation regulatory information
   b) Applying optical character recognition to extract text content
   c) Utilizing artificial intelligence algorithms to identify and extract regulatory fields
   d) Generating confidence scores for extracted data accuracy
   e) Outputting structured regulatory data for compliance management

2. The method of claim 1, wherein the artificial intelligence processing utilizes OpenAI GPT-4o language models with aviation-specific prompt engineering for regulatory field identification and extraction.

3. The method of claim 1, wherein FAA pilot certificate processing includes Roman numeral section parsing for extracting certificate numbers, ratings, and limitations from sections I through XXVI.

4. The method of claim 1, further comprising automated validation of extracted data against Federal Aviation Regulation requirements and FAA database cross-referencing.

5. The method of claim 1, wherein confidence scoring utilizes multi-factor assessment including text clarity, field consistency, and regulatory validation to generate accuracy percentages.

6. A system for aviation regulatory document processing comprising:
   a) Document upload interface for receiving regulatory documents
   b) OCR processing module for text extraction from images and PDFs
   c) AI processing engine utilizing natural language processing for field extraction
   d) Validation module for regulatory compliance verification
   e) Structured data output interface for integration with compliance systems

7. The system of claim 6, wherein the AI processing engine implements specialized aviation regulatory knowledge for accurate field identification across diverse document formats.

8. The system of claim 6, further comprising multi-language processing capabilities for international aviation document support and ICAO standard compliance.

9. The system of claim 6, wherein the validation module includes automated error detection and correction for common OCR processing errors in aviation documents.

10. A computer-readable medium containing instructions for implementing the aviation regulatory document processing method of claims 1-5.

ABSTRACT

An AI-powered system for processing aviation regulatory documents that automatically extracts, validates, and structures data from pilot certificates, training records, and regulatory documents using advanced natural language processing. The system utilizes OpenAI GPT-4o with aviation-specific prompting to achieve 95%+ accuracy in extracting regulatory fields, including specialized processing for FAA certificate Roman numeral sections and multi-language international document support. The invention provides confidence scoring, automated validation, and structured output for seamless integration with aviation compliance management systems.

